The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ctx = blk_mq_get_ctx(q);
hctx = blk_mq_map_queue(q, ctx->cpu);
data->hctx = hctx;
```
Reason:
When the system runs out of requests and sleeps, the context (`ctx`) and hardware context (`hctx`) are not updated after waking up. As a result, `data->hctx` continues to point to the pre-sleep context, which can lead to incorrect locking when inserting requests into `ctx->rq_list`, risking data corruption.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
data->hctx = alloc_data.hctx;
data->ctx = alloc_data.ctx;
hctx->queued++;
```
Reason:
The patch updates `data->hctx` and `data->ctx` with the values from `alloc_data`, which are correctly set after the request allocation. This ensures that the correct context is used after potentially sleeping, preventing the risk of data corruption by maintaining the integrity of the request queue and its associated locks.

